Euclids Algorithms for GCD- 

        1. Euclid’s  Lemma-  Suppose d divides both m, n. Then m = ad, n = bd
        so m-n = ad- bd = (a-b)d this implies d divides m-n as well
        
        Euclid’s Algorithm-  
        a. consider gcd(m, n) with m>n
        b. if n divides m, return n
        c. otherwise compute gcd(n, m-n) and return that value
        def gcd(m,n):
          if m < n:
            (m,n) = (n,m)
        
          if (m%n) == 0:
            return(n)
          else:
            diff = m-n
            return(gcd(max(n, diff),min(n, diff))
        
        
        replacing the recursive call using a while loop - 
        
        def gcd(m, n):
        if m<n:
        	(m, n) = (n, m)
        while (m%n) != 0
